{
  "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
  "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Deputy Solicitor General Eric J. Feigin)",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Indian tribes, like other sovereigns, have the core inherent authority to investigate and detain suspects within their borders for the violation of another sovereign's law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Deputy Solicitor General Eric J. Feigin)",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The holding lacks any meaningful support, substantially chills tribes' ability even to enforce their own laws against their own members, and endangers everyone on Indian reservations. It should be reversed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would have thought Montana said the exact opposite. You know, you do argue at the outset there's this inherent authority and nothing took it away."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Feigin, do you think you could offer us a general test for distinguishing between those aspects of sovereignty that tribes retained and those that they did not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My question approaching it that way, Mr. Feigin, is, where is the line? The Major Crimes Act clearly precludes states or --or tribes from trying certain individuals, non-native persons, for -- for major crimes in Indian country."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. FEIGIN",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So I think the line would be around where we have described it in our briefs, which is a limited detention and investigatory authority that's simply for the purpose of allowing state or federal authorities at some point to take over and conduct an arrest."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. FEIGIN",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't think that tribes have been understood to have the authority to conduct arrests on their own."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I guess my question remains, does that come from the Constitution, or how does that fit within the Constitution?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BARRETT",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You said that the authority -- the investigative authority doesn't extend past Terry stops into arrests because arrests mark the beginning of the adjudicatory process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. FEIGIN",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "non-Indians cannot be subject to tribal adjudication is one line of demarcation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. HENKEL",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case is resolved by the fundamental propositions that Indian tribes do not possess sovereign authority over non-Indians and that Congress has plenary authority over Indian affairs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Henkel",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HENKEL: I -- I think, if the conduct rises to the level of a potential, you know, ongoing active breach of the peace where public safety is in jeopardy, I think, in that circumstance, that would fit under the Ninth Circuit's apparent standard."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, if\nthey're not authorized by law to make -- to do\ninvestigations, why are they subject to the\nFourth Amendment --\nMR. HENKEL: Well, they're not\nstrictly --\nJUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: -- to the Fourth\nAmendment's exclusionary rule?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Henkel",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HENKEL: Yes, they would."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Henkel",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HENKEL: I don't think there would be any remedy in terms of a private cause of action for civil damages. Certainly, tribal officers aren't mentioned in 1983. You can't bring a claim -- claim against a tribe because they have sovereign immunity. You could potentially try to sue the tribe in tribal court, but the likelihood of that being successful is -- is not very good. And, ultimately, in that -- in that situation, even if you could sue them in tribal court, you can't get it into state or federal court, so this Court doesn't sit at the end of the line there. So I think there's very -- there's virtually no remedy other than exclusion of evidence in this circumstance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So why isn't the best thing we can do here just to stick with what we said in those cases?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Cooley)",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Cooley does not challenge tribal sovereignty. He simply asks that the boundaries of tribal sovereignty be respected as this Court has previously defined them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Feigin)",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Second, cross-designation is simply not a solution. If you look at our brief and the Cayuga Nation brief, they detail the problems with that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Feigin)",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They say that you can detain someone who matches the description of a serial killer. Well, how sure do you have to be that he matches the description of the serial killer?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1414",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "0369eb1be177bacb906cd31349e9a3af083fb9dde271f1f6e92dc78e66a21b47",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0369eb1be177-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
